1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,548
Some content is meant for one team only.

2
00:00:03,548 --> 00:00:07,923
This video shows how Content Access Control limits who can view a content

3
00:00:07,923 --> 00:00:10,471
item to the roles you pick on that item:

4
00:00:10,471 --> 00:00:13,794
why it exists, how to set it up on a content type, how

5
00:00:13,794 --> 00:00:16,840
to restrict an item, and how to check the result.

6
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:23,962
Some pages are not for everyone:

7
00:00:23,962 --> 00:00:29,670
a supervisor handbook, an internal price list, or notes for a single department.

8
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:35,091
Permissions normally apply to a whole content type, so two pages of the

9
00:00:35,091 --> 00:00:37,760
same type are open to the same people.

10
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:44,700
Content Access Control lets the editor choose, on each item, the roles that may view it.

11
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:50,900
Everyone else is refused that item, and the rest of the site stays open as before.

12
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:59,157
It builds on the Role Picker part, which lets an editor pick one

13
00:00:59,157 --> 00:01:01,360
or more roles on a content item.

14
00:01:02,110 --> 00:01:08,690
On the content type, one setting, Restrict content, turns the picker into an access rule.

15
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:12,854
A person can view an item only if they hold at least one

16
00:01:12,854 --> 00:01:14,286
of the picked roles.

17
00:01:14,286 --> 00:01:17,480
An item with no roles picked stays open to everyone.

18
00:01:18,230 --> 00:01:20,119
Only viewing is limited.

19
00:01:20,119 --> 00:01:25,346
Who can edit, publish or delete the item still follows the usual permissions,

20
00:01:25,346 --> 00:01:28,620
and administrators can always view every item.

21
00:01:32,778 --> 00:01:39,725
Open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit the type that needs restricted items.

22
00:01:39,725 --> 00:01:41,878
Here it is Handbook Page.

23
00:01:42,331 --> 00:01:43,756
Click Add Parts.

24
00:01:43,756 --> 00:01:49,457
Role Picker is in the list, described as allowing you to select one or more roles.

25
00:01:49,457 --> 00:01:51,401
Click Add and Configure.

26
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:55,342
The Display Name is what editors see above the picker.

27
00:01:55,342 --> 00:01:59,230
Give it a clear name, such as Limit access to selected roles.

28
00:01:59,681 --> 00:02:05,773
Exclude roles hides the roles that should never be picked, such as Anonymous and Authenticated.

29
00:02:05,773 --> 00:02:08,668
Required means an editor must pick a role.

30
00:02:08,668 --> 00:02:12,951
Allow multiple lets an editor pick more than one, and the Hint is

31
00:02:12,951 --> 00:02:14,941
help text under the picker.

32
00:02:15,392 --> 00:02:19,000
Restrict content turns the picker into an access rule:

33
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,488
only people in the selected roles can view the item.

34
00:02:22,488 --> 00:02:23,932
Tick it, and save.

35
00:02:28,139 --> 00:02:33,469
Open Content, Content Items, and create a new Handbook Page.

36
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:42,813
Give the page a title, such as Supervisor handbook, and type its text.

37
00:02:42,813 --> 00:02:45,420
The role picker is below the text.

38
00:02:45,890 --> 00:02:49,818
The picker shows the hint, and lists the roles of the site.

39
00:02:49,818 --> 00:02:53,868
Search for a role, and tick the ones that may view this page.

40
00:02:53,868 --> 00:02:55,560
Here it is Supervisor.

41
00:02:56,129 --> 00:02:57,627
Publish the page.

42
00:02:57,627 --> 00:03:02,319
From now on, only people who hold the Supervisor role can view it.

43
00:03:03,753 --> 00:03:08,821
To lift the restriction from one page, untick all its roles and save.

44
00:03:08,821 --> 00:03:14,363
To lift it from every page of the type, untick Restrict content on the part.

45
00:03:18,663 --> 00:03:22,306
Always check the result by signing in as other people.

46
00:03:22,306 --> 00:03:25,221
Casey Morgan holds the Support Agent role.

47
00:03:25,221 --> 00:03:29,533
The Support hours page has no roles picked, so Casey can open it.

48
00:03:29,988 --> 00:03:34,220
The Supervisor handbook is restricted to the Supervisor role.

49
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:37,568
Casey does not hold it, so the page is refused.

50
00:03:38,028 --> 00:03:43,598
Jordan Lee holds the Supervisor role, so the same address opens the handbook.

51
00:03:47,798 --> 00:03:53,298
A supervisor handbook or an escalation guide that only supervisors should read.

52
00:03:54,048 --> 00:03:57,988
An internal price list or discount rules for the sales team.

53
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:04,158
Documents for one partner or one department, each limited to its own role.

54
00:04:04,908 --> 00:04:08,388
Announcements and procedures for a single team.

55
00:04:10,388 --> 00:04:15,110
Set up the Role Picker once on a content type, and turn on Restrict content.

56
00:04:15,110 --> 00:04:18,622
Then every page of that type can have its own audience:

57
00:04:18,622 --> 00:04:22,307
pick the roles on an item, and only people who hold one of

58
00:04:22,307 --> 00:04:23,631
them can view it.

59
00:04:23,631 --> 00:04:25,128
Thanks for watching.

